        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T20:05:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should take `sizeOfT` into account; we don\u0027t ever need fractions of a T. Even if it was totally free to round up (which isn\u0027t a given), we\u0027ll still never use it so we shouldn\u0027t request it.\n\nExample: if `atLeast\u003d1` and `sizeOfT\u003d1MB` and `growthFactor\u003d1.5`, I think this will give us a 1.5MB allocation. That 0.5MB of space goes unused because it\u0027s too small to hold a T. Obviously that\u0027s an extreme example, but it would still apply to `sizeOfT\u003d5K` or something.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "49cff8c93d95c8d2469846a4a3934b31875dc9f0",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a55d0ec_69bd14a1",
        "filename": "include/private/SkMalloc.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
